C(33,[46,47],'false as stated','ForTU=[[1,0],[U,1]], TU^−1=T−U, whereas−T−U has diagonal−1. AtU=0 overZ the claimed equality identifiesI with−I. Also(−b1)(−b2)=+b1b2, which is not the same convention as output coefficient−b.','F','The literal chains fail under a single fixed endpoint convention. The surviving signs may involve a changed identification, so ink and notation review are needed before assigning an intended theorem. No modern paper can decide this textual ambiguity.',['Loos1997','Pirashvili2019'],['Q04'])
C(34,[49],'stated without proof','extension_checks.json enumeratesγχ=2 overZ/4 forχ=2:γ=1,3. Forb=1 the resultingv are3,1, distinct translations whose difference2 isχ-annihilated.','D','The displayed recipe depends on the chosenγ in general. This rechecks an earlier-run example, not an authorial claim of noncanonicity. Searches of the parameterized torsor literature give related categorical structures but do not supply a canonical choice for arbitrary extensions.',['Pirashvili2019'],['Q04'],statement='Earlier-run observation: different solutions ofγχ=2 can give distinct strict-endpoint comparisons v=−γb; the condition alone does not define a unique comparison.')
C(35,[50],'false as stated','Expand(b1+χU1)(b2+χU2)−b1b2=χ(b1U2+U1b2+χU1U2)=χU. Literal final+U in the same coordinates has defect(χ−1)U; e.g.χ=2,b1=1,b2=U1=0,U2=1 overZ gives2≠1.','F','The product coefficient identity is exact. The final displayed line needs either a factorχ or an explicit coordinate transport; its intended reading cannot be chosen without scans.',['Loos1997'],['Q04'])
C(36,[51,53],'proof sketched','ForU(b,u)=b1u2+u1b2+χu1u2 andb′=b+χu, expansion givesU(b,u+v)=U(b,u)+U(b′,v). With the mixed minus branch the residual is2χ(u1v2+u2v1), nonzero atχ=u1=v2=1,u2=v1=0 overZ.','C','A coherent local cocycle is established here. Loos1997 §2.8(3) gives the χ=2 quadratic-form analogue with its own sign convention and §2.10 supplies coherence for quadratic algebras. General χ-extension monoidal coherence is stronger than the single worksheet cocycle.',['Loos1997','Pirashvili2019'],['Q04'])
C(37,[55],'open on the pages','IfL is invertible thenEnd(L)=R, so the scalar restriction of anyf is unique. Without faithfulness, f|L=λid may hold for severalλ; forL=R/I,λ andλ+i give the same restriction. Using pairs(f,λ) repairs this ambiguity. Undefined primed brackets cannot be checked further without a type assignment.','F','The special-dual notation is unfinished locally. The invertible-line version is standard; a unique arbitrary-module object cannot be recovered from the displayed set builder. The later notation must not be imported silently.',['Loos1997'],['Q04'])
C(38,[56,57],'proved there','Forfi=a_iη_i+λ_iζ_i andπ_i=b_iη_i+χζ_i, the functional formula equals(λ1b1a2+λ2a1b2−χa1a2)η1η2+λ1λ2(b1η1ζ2+b2ζ1η2+χζ1ζ2). It therefore descends and agrees withλ1λ2 on the scalar-boundary generator. Both mixed strata and overlap checked in extension_checks.json.','C','The local functional product is valid and includes the product splitting. Loos’s quadratic-product cocycle is a close χ=2 counterpart; the exact general χ-extension functional formula was not located as a published theorem in the bounded search.',['Loos1997','Pirashvili2019'],['Q04'])
